Package: LFQPCA
Type: Package
Title: Longitudinal Functional Quantile Principal Component Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ufuk", "Beyaztas", email = "ufuk.beyaztas@marmara.edu.tr",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5208-4950"))
Description: Longitudinal functional quantile principal component analysis
    (LFQPCA) decomposes the conditional quantiles of curves recorded at
    repeated visits into a population surface, persistent subject
    trajectories with functional intercepts and slopes in time, and transient
    visit deviations that carry no trend within a subject. Longitudinal
    functional quantile principal component regression (LFQPCR) relates the
    quantiles of a scalar response to the two fitted components through
    separate coefficient functions. Estimation minimizes a subject-balanced
    check loss over spline bases. The package includes prediction for new
    subjects, cross-validation, a subject bootstrap and the data-generating
    designs of the simulation study in the accompanying paper.
